Congratulations - your keynote has been
confirmed for IEEE WICS 2027. This message
summarizes travel arrangements and what
happens next. No action is needed before
the speaker portal opens.

1. CONFERENCE & SESSION DETAILS

  Conference:      IEEE WICS 2027 (Workshop
                   on Intelligent & Connected
                   Systems)
  Venue / dates:   Suntec Singapore,
                   14-18 March 2027
  Your role:       Keynote, Session AI-4:
                   "Federated Learning at
                   Industrial Scale"
                   (paper 4471-AI)
  Keynote slot:    15 March, 09:30-10:30
  Honorarium:      USD 2,500 (paid after
                   the conference by wire,
                   W-8BEN required)
  Travel grant:    Economy round-trip +
                   4 hotel nights

2. HOW TRAVEL IS ACTUALLY ARRANGED

    1. The speaker portal opens next week.
       Access it by typing the conference
       address yourself (it is printed in
       your acceptance letter) and log in
       with your IEEE account.
    2. Inside the portal you confirm
       arrival/departure preferences and
       dietary needs. Flights and hotel
       are booked by the organizing
       committee's designated travel
       agency, which will contact you
       from its own verifiable corporate
       address to ticket the booking.
    3. Visa support letters are issued
       on IEEE letterhead directly from
       the portal (upload passport scan
       INSIDE the portal only).

  The conference will NEVER:
  - Email a "pre-linked" portal session
    that opens without your IEEE login
  - Collect passport scans, W-8BEN, or
    bank details through email forms
    or non-IEEE domains
  - Operate a "consulate partner desk"
    or "consular fast-track" channel
    for expedited visas outside the
    official portal
  - Pressure you with fare-holding
    deadlines in the same message that
    asks for identity documents
    (the designated agency holds fares
    after the portal confirms your
    session, and grant allocations are
    never "reverted to standby" over
    a week's delay)

3. VERIFY THIS MESSAGE

  - Compare the sender domain with the
    one in your acceptance letter
  - Keynote confirmations are also
    mirrored in the speaker portal
    (typed address)
  - When in doubt, write to the TPC
    chair using the address on the
    conference Call for Papers page

4. TIMELINE

  Portal opens:      next week
  Travel confirmed:  within 2 weeks of
                     portal submission
  Visa letters:      issued from the
                     portal, 5 business
                     days
  Honorarium:        within 30 days
